  "question": {
    "text": "An object is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from a convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. On the other side of the lens, a convex mirror is placed at its focus such that the image by the combination coincides with the object itself. What is the focal length (in cm) of the convex mirror?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/KT0000339_Question_1_.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 137px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
